From 34ae6f5e35a16186422a4f93cdae617ed7221927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Bitzek <e.bitzek@mpie.de>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 13:29:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] Add compute sites/voronoi/kk: sync device atoms to host
 before tessellation

Kokkos-aware subclass selected by -sf kk.  The tessellation, clustering
and site criteria stay on the host (Voro++ is a serial CPU library); the
subclass only pulls live positions/type/mask/tag off the device with
atomKK->sync(Host, ...) before the host reads them.  Fixes the empty
catalogue (Msites=0) seen under -sf kk on devices with separate memory.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0183gtTmwDnCVQWCaTxG4HPQ
---
 src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.cpp | 46 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.h   | 38 +++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 84 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.cpp
 create mode 100644 src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.h

diff --git a/src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.cpp b/src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0376a3b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/KOKKOS/compute_sites_voronoi_kokkos.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
